remstart
    THE WANTED SHAPE, AND THE CATCH
    another hidden thing, and a prototype. the routines are in fish_routines_wanted, and the tests are in
    fish_tests_wanted. nothing in the game says that it is there.

    THE SHAPE. at any time, one shape of four fish is wanted: an L, a T, an S, a square or a line, in that
    order, over and over. it moves on to the next one every time that it is popped. a new game starts at
    the L. the order is always the same, and no roll is taken for it, so a seed plays the same.

    THE BUBBLES SHOW IT. when a group of fish that matched pops, some of the bubbles that come up from it do
    not scatter: one bubble for each fish of the wanted shape comes up from the middle of the group, all of
    them together, in that shape, a little bigger than the rest, in the color of the fish. they are not
    lined up exactly: each one is a little out of its place (WANTED_JITTER), a little bigger or smaller,
    comes up a little faster or slower, and wobbles a little out of time with the others. after a while
    they pop, one and then another, over WANTED_LIFE_SPREAD, like any bubbles. so whatever is popped, the
    bubbles that come up from it make the same shape, and that is all the hint that there is. the shape is
    shown turned whichever way has the fewest rows. WANTED_GAP# is how far apart the bubbles are, as a share
    of a cell. a forced pop does not send any up. see wantedBubbles.

    A CATCH. a group of fish that matched, and pops, in the wanted shape is a catch, turned any of the four
    ways round, and flipped over or not: an L is caught as a J too, and an S as a Z. it has to be exactly
    that shape, four fish, no more. it lights up before it pops: the colors of the rainbow flood through its
    fish, in a wave that crosses the screen, and their edges shimmer in them, the way that a jellyfish's do
    at night (see THE RAINBOW FLOOD in FishEffect.fx). a burst goes off at each of its cells in turn, along
    a walk of the shape: bubbles in the next color of the rainbow, little stars, and a ring through the
    fish. the specks in the water are the colors of the rainbow too, a chord rings, and "x+1" pops up over
    the group, the way that a score does, in all of the colors of the rainbow (RainbowTextEffect.fx), and
    floats up while it waits. handle_combos holds
    its pops, and every pop after them, for WANTED_HOLD. when it pops, it scores what it would have, and the
    multiplier goes up by one, and its bar is emptied, as if it had been filled. then the next shape is
    wanted. wantedCatchAhead, which handle_combos calls before the groups pop, finds the group, and
    wantedCaught lights it up.

    AT NIGHT nothing pops, so the shape that was wanted when night fell is wanted all night, and no bubbles
    show it. every group that the night held pops at once when day breaks, and only one of them can be a
    catch: so the night is one chance at one catch, of the last shape that was shown.
remend

global WANTED_ON = 1 `0 turns all of this off, for the debug window

` THE SHAPES, four fish each, as column + row * 4, shown the way round that has the fewest rows
global WANTED_SHAPE_COUNT = 5
global WANTED_SHAPE_SIZE = 4
global dim WANTED_SHAPES(20)
global WANTED_SHAPE = 0 `which one is wanted now
global WANTED_WIDE = 1 `how many columns it takes, and how many rows
global WANTED_DEEP = 1

` every shape turned the four ways round, and flipped over and turned the four ways again, as column +
` row * 4, in the order of the board, row by row: 32 for each shape, 4 for each way
global WANTED_WAYS = 8
global dim WANTED_ROTS(160)

` what wantedTurnShape works out, one shape turned one way: the cells in order, and how many rows it takes
global dim WANTED_TURN_CODE(4)
global dim WANTED_TURN_COLUMN(4)
global dim WANTED_TURN_ROW(4)
global WANTED_TURN_DEEP = 0

` A CATCH. the group in the wanted shape, while handle_combos pops it, or -1, and how many times as much it
` scores. for each group, while they are looked at: how many of its fish have been seen, the first of
` them, and 1 for each way round that one of them is not where the shape would have it.
global WANTED_CATCH_GROUP = -1
global WANTED_MULT_DUE = 0 `when the multiplier of a catch goes up, on the clock of the game, or 0
global WANTED_CATCHES = 0 `how many there have been, for the debug window and the tests
global dim WANTED_G_SEEN(400)
global dim WANTED_G_ANCHOR(400)
global dim WANTED_G_BAD(3200)

` THE BUBBLES. how far apart they are, as a share of a cell, how big, how fast they come up, in pixels a
` second, how long they last, in milliseconds, and how solid they are, out of 255
global WANTED_GAP# = .7
global WANTED_BUBBLE_SIZE = 12
global WANTED_RISE = 30
global WANTED_LIFE = 2400
global WANTED_ALPHA = 230
global WANTED_AFTER = 150 `how long after the pop the shape comes up, so that the puff of the pop is out of the way
global WANTED_JITTER = 2 `how many pixels each bubble can be out of its place, either way
global WANTED_RISE_SPREAD = 10 `how much faster or slower each one comes up, in pixels a second, either way
global WANTED_LIFE_SPREAD = 900 `the bubbles pop one after another, over this many milliseconds
global WANTED_FORMATIONS = 0 `how many shapes of bubbles have gone up, for the tests

` THE LIGHT OF A CATCH. the cells of the group, the walk of the bursts through them, which goes back over
` a cell where the shape branches, and how long it takes to go from one cell to the next
global dim WANTED_CELLS(4)
global dim WANTED_WALK(8)
global WANTED_WALK_COUNT = 0
global dim WANTED_WALK_SEEN(4)
global dim WANTED_WALK_STACK(8)
global WANTED_HINT_STEP = 450
global WANTED_RAINBOW_UNTIL = 0 `the specks are all the colors of the rainbow until then, on the clock of the game
global WANTED_RAINBOW_FROM = 0

` THE PULSE. as the light gets to each cell of the walk, there is a burst there: bubbles in one color of the
` rainbow, a color further along it for every step, little stars that twinkle, and a ring that goes out
` through the fish. see wantedPulse.
global dim WANTED_HUES(6)
global WANTED_PULSE_BUBBLES = 7
global WANTED_PULSE_STARS = 5
global WANTED_PULSE_SHOCK# = .45
global WANTED_LIGHT_FROM = 0 `when the light set out, on the clock of the game
global WANTED_LIGHT_NEXT = 0 `the step of the walk that is the next to burst
global WANTED_HOLD = 0 `how long the pops wait for the light to go through the group, worked out by wantedLight
` the fish that the rainbow floods: 1 for each cell of a group in the wanted shape, until WANTED_SHIMMER_UNTIL
global dim WANTED_SHIMMERS(400)
global WANTED_SHIMMER_UNTIL = 0
` THE RAINBOW FLOOD. how far along its wave a pixel of the screen is, across and down. FishEffect.fx has
` these too, as RAINBOW_WAVE, and the two have to be kept the same by hand. the band of light goes from
` the near end of the group to the far end, once, while its pops wait, and it is WANTED_WAVE_WIDE# wide.
global WANTED_WAVE_X# = .006
global WANTED_WAVE_Y# = .0035
global WANTED_WAVE_WIDE# = .12
global WANTED_WAVE_FROM# = 0
global WANTED_WAVE_TO# = 0


` THE TEXT OF A CATCH. "x+1", drawn to a render target of its own, which RainbowTextEffect.fx draws over the
` board. where it is, when it pops up and when it is gone, on the clock of the game, and how tall it is.
global TARGET_WANTED_TEXT = 0
global WANTED_TEXT_FX_ID = 0
global WANTED_TEXT_SPRITE = 0
global WANTED_TEXT_ID = 0
global WANTED_TEXT_X# = 0
global WANTED_TEXT_Y# = 0
global WANTED_TEXT_FROM = 0
global WANTED_TEXT_UNTIL = 0
global WANTED_TEXT_HEIGHT = 30
global WANTED_TEXT_RISE = 14
